rlbosses. Hold the line, sir.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 42275}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV8A11xE", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 17, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8816914, "raw_content": "", "author": "FREN", "created": 1788529660252, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "HeDinduNuffin", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATV8A11xE.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/jvK1Fm5FgUEq.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/qtxlM2MKutKmqmmQ.jpeg", "width": 768, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 594}], "blurhash": "UHJQl[0Y?pZ6{@YfMf?Fv=KQnpxUNHIn-zR=", "full_resolution": [836, 1080]}, "title": "sorry it had to come to this...", "last_comment_created": 1788533513376, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 5, "score_up": 17, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATV8A0lNA", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 18, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8816888, "raw_content": "I've spent several years now in the kitchen as a stay-at-home dad.\n\nI've cooked way too many pancakes, cookies, pies, and cakes to count.  In almost every recipe, there's a teaspoon or so of vanilla extract.\n\nVanilla extract is rather expensive, so one day I simply stopped adding it.  Strangely, there was zero change in the taste of the final product.  So, I stopped buying vanilla extract altogether.\n\nIs there some sort of vanilla extract lobby attempting to ensure continuous consumption of this seemingly flavorless flavor?  Or have I just been using flavorless vanilla without understanding what actual vanilla tastes like?\n\nSomeone once told me that freshly ground or scraped vanilla bean definitely adds flavor... and that one only needs a tiny sample of the freshly procured vanilla bean scrapings to make a big difference in the taste of the final product.\n\nPerhaps.... like so many other things in \"modern\" life.... vanilla extract is simply a placeholder for a meaningless tasteless ingredient meant to feel like something meaningful.\n\nThe king has no clothes.... and vanilla extract actually has no flavor.\n\n-- End Mini-Wall of Meaningless Text ---", "author": "24601", "created": 1788528523876, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Elencher", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Why does vanilla extract have zero flavor?", "last_comment_created": 1788533357088, "content": "<p>I've spent several years now in the kitchen as a stay-at-home dad.</p>\n<p>I've cooked way too many pancakes, cookies, pies, and cakes to count.  In almost every recipe, there's a teaspoon or so of vanilla extract.</p>\n<p>Vanilla extract is rather expensive, so one day I simply stopped adding it.  Strangely, there was zero change in the taste of the final product.  So, I stopped buying vanilla extract altogether.</p>\n<p>Is there some sort of vanilla extract lobby attempting to ensure continuous consumption of this seemingly flavorless flavor?  Or have I just been using flavorless vanilla without understanding what actual vanilla tastes like?</p>\n<p>Someone once told me that freshly ground or scraped vanilla bean definitely adds flavor... and that one only needs a tiny sample of the freshly procured vanilla bean scrapings to make a big difference in the taste of the final product.</p>\n<p>Perhaps.... like so many other things in &quot;modern&quot; life.... vanilla extract is simply a placeholder for a meaningless tasteless ingredient meant to feel like something meaningful.</p>\n<p>The king has no clothes.... and vanilla extract actually has no flavor.</p>\n<p>-- End Mini-Wall of Meaningless Text ---</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 15, "score_up": 18, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV88sdlg", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 259, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8815968, "raw_content": "", "author": "China4Biden", "created": 1788476240836, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "KungPaoMcChicken", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.patriots.win", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATV88sdlg.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.patriots.win/post/UMZduBoYMgNc.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/Ydlh9CYREj8hLVe3.jpeg", "width": 768, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 757}], "blurhash": "UKOM{ZRj00Mx00kC9FoJ~pbb%2t7?^WVxuW;", "full_resolution": [1063, 1079]}, "title": "Based Mel Gibson > Woke Christopher Nolan. Hacksaw Ridge was a far superior WWII film compared to Dunkirk!!", "l